From: phaer <hello@phaer.org>
Subject: [PATCH] panic: flush the consoles after the "Rebooting in" line

panic() flushes the consoles with console_flush_on_panic(), which
ignores the console lock, and only then prints "Rebooting in %d
seconds..". That printk prints only when the panic CPU gets the console
lock. When another context holds it, for example a task that writes to
a VT and was stopped or preempted, the line stays in the buffer and no
console shows it before the reboot.

Flush the consoles once more after the line, as the panic_timeout == 0
path already does after its last line.

Upstream: not sent
Assisted-by: Claude Code (claude-opus-5-5)
---
 kernel/panic.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/panic.c b/kernel/panic.c
--- a/kernel/panic.c
+++ b/kernel/panic.c
@@ -561,6 +561,11 @@
 		 * We can't use the "normal" timers since we just panicked.
 		 */
 		pr_emerg("Rebooting in %d seconds..\n", panic_timeout);
+		/*
+		 * The flush above ignored the console lock. If another
+		 * context holds it, the printk above only stored the line.
+		 */
+		console_flush_on_panic(CONSOLE_FLUSH_PENDING);
 
 		for (i = 0; i < panic_timeout * 1000; i += PANIC_TIMER_STEP) {
 			touch_nmi_watchdog();
